{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Both $81$ and $4x^2$ are *perfect squares,* since $81=(\\blueD{9})^2$ and $4x^2=(\\greenD{2x})^2$.\n\n$81-4x^2 = (\\blueD{9})^2-(\\greenD{2x})^2$\n\nSo we can use the *difference of squares* pattern to factor.\n\n$\\blueD{a}^2 - \\greenD{b}^2 =(\\blueD{a}+\\greenD{b})(\\blueD{a}-\\greenD{b})$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this case, $\\blueD{a}=\\blueD{9}$ and $\\greenD{b}=\\greenD{2x}$:\n\n$(\\blueD{9})^2 - (\\greenD{2x})^2 =(\\blueD{9}+\\greenD{2x})(\\blueD{9}-\\greenD{2x})$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$81-4x^2=(9+2x)(9-2x)$\n\n*Remember that you can always check your factorization by expanding it.*","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Factor completely.**\n\n$81-4x^2=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"(9+2x)(9-2x)"},{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":1,"simplify":false,"value":"-(2x+9)(2x-9)"}],"buttonSets":["basic"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
